{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS Query Model.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS Query Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cqrs query model cqrs query model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS Query Model.md","fileName":"CQRS Query Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CQRS Query Model","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CQRS and Ledger Data Architecture]] [[CQRS Query and Read Model Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CQRS and Ledger Data Architecture","CQRS Query and Read Model Design","Read Model Ubiquitous Language","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS Query Model.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS Query Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cqrs query model cqrs query model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CQRS Query Model.md","fileName":"CQRS Query Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CQRS Query Model","heading":"CQRS Query Model","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A CQRS query model supplies data without changing application state. The book models requests for all products and for one product as distinct query types with handlers that retrieve their responses. A read model may use different fields, indexing, or even a separate store from the command side, giving callers a representation suited to retrieval rather than to write validation.\n\nQuery models should be shaped around the information a user or external system needs to make a decision. They can join information from multiple aggregates, use a [[Read Model Ubiquitous Language]], and return the stored representation directly. This avoids loading behavioral aggregates solely to display data.","tags":["baby"],"links":[